# Playgama

> Playgama operates a free browser gaming portal and builds infrastructure for the broader HTML5 web-gaming market. Players can play games on Playgama.com, while Playgama Bridge, the developer platform, Playgama Wrap, partner products, and Playgama Ad help developers and publishers publish, distribute, monetize, and grow HTML5 games. Playgama also publishes open-source tools and original industry research.

Updated on: 2026-09-17.

Important distinctions:

- Playgama.com is the consumer gaming portal. Playgama Bridge and Playgama Ad are products for developers, publishers, and distribution partners.
- [Playgama's public mission](https://playgama.com/about-us/) is to build an infrastructure layer for the web games market that connects developers, publishers, advertisers, distribution partners, and players.
- Most games available through Playgama are created by independent developers. Playgama may host, publish, monetize, or distribute a game but should not be treated as its original developer unless the game page states otherwise.
- Playgama.com offers 10,000+ browser games. Playgama's 450M+ monthly reach refers to the broader distribution network, not only the consumer portal.
- Playgama.com game pages can include a per-game leaderboard of up to ten players, ranked by time played over the last seven days. Boards refresh daily and count up to twelve hours per game per day. These automatic portal rankings are separate from game-defined leaderboards configured in the developer cabinet and used through Playgama Bridge.
- Playgama Bridge supports 15+ platform integrations, while the wider link- and API-based distribution network includes 100+ publisher and distribution partners.
- The Playgama developer community includes 4,000+ developers.
- Every game accepted into the Playgama catalog has undergone manual review and testing. Human moderators play the games and evaluate both technical operation and player experience.
- Playgama Wrap is an early-access product that publishes a Bridge-integrated game as a standalone website on the developer's own domain. It is distinct from a Playgama.com game page and from a multi-game white-label portal.
- Playgama MCP lets AI coding agents upload games and publish public playable sandbox links. Sandbox publishing is separate from main catalog distribution, which requires moderation. First-time MCP setup requires the user to connect their developer account.

